{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1285676-dots-points-and-the-wonder-background","id":1285676,"title":"Dots, Points, and the Wonder Background","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-07T13:59:26-08:00","id":1285676,"title":"Dots, Points, and the Wonder Background","content":"Can anyone help break down the Wonder Background for me? I mean, I get that such-and-such Dot rating equals a Wonder worth such-and-such points, but how do we determine how many points a Wonders effect(s) are worth? And why is it that several of the example Wonders in the book have point values that don't match with their Dot ratings? It is all very confusing to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T07:17:15-08:00","id":1285880,"title":"","content":"The highest Sphere level employed for the effects determine the cost. For instance: A Wonder with a Life 3 power to heal the body of others and a distinct Mind 5 power to heal the mind of others it's worth 10 Background points (5 if it's a Charm with limited uses).<br /> <br /> Other things can modify this assertion. Like Arete (a Wonder with a single Life 3 effect and Arete 4 cost 8/4 points) or the amount of effects (a Wonder with 3 spells will cost at least 6/3 points) OR Defects included as part of the Bacground (a cursed Wonder reduces it's value one dot per dot of the Defect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T07:36:45-08:00","id":1285886,"title":"","content":"I believe this is one the rules of the game that most could use a rework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6470-sardonis","name":"Sardonis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T06:42:44-08:00","id":1293734,"title":"","content":"The m20 core says 1 to 3 &quot;points&quot; per dot... amd then pretty much costs things out at 2 points per dot. And sometimes not even that. I don't get it myself. I assume 2 background or freebies per dot is the basic cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:21:03-08:00","id":1294036,"title":"","content":"The book just needed to make a formula for Wonder cost, and give each of the examples a Freebie value. As is the system is very... confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T09:38:09-08:00","id":1294090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1285676-dots-points-and-the-wonder-background?p=1294036#post1294036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book just needed to make a formula for Wonder cost, and give each of the examples a Freebie value. As is the system is very... confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What they should have done was a quick line at the bottom explaining how the costing out worked. Then players would have guidelines they could follow. Unfortunately, while Phil Brucato writes amazing fluff and is a very creative guy... Mechanics and rule consistency are not his strong point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T10:01:22-08:00","id":1294093,"title":"","content":"This is a question I asked too. They don't seem to follow their own rules for creation, but i guess that's because they don't need to be followed if you don't want. I just don't understand why a mage would create a wonder with only 2 effects while he could create it with 4 for the same costs, for example. <br /> <br /> Even though they don't follow their rules, the rules are very clear. Wonders cost 2 bg points for each dot in the highest sphere of its effects. They also have 1 Arete for each dot (you can buy more Arete with 1 bg point), 5 quintessence and one effect for each dot.<br /> So, a wonder with a Life 4+Forces 2 effect, a Correspondence 3 effect, a Forces 1 effect and a Prime 3 effect would cost 8 background points because of the Life 4 effect, would have Arete 4 and 20 quintessence.<br /> <br /> About the points system described in the background section, there is absolutely no sense in that and I advise you to just ignore it and go by the rules on the wonder section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T15:25:22-08:00","id":1294188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1285676-dots-points-and-the-wonder-background?p=1294093#post1294093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question I asked too. They don't seem to follow their own rules for creation, but i guess that's because they don't need to be followed if you don't want. I just don't understand why a mage would create a wonder with only 2 effects while he could create it with 4 for the same costs, for example.<br /> <br /> Even though they don't follow their rules, the rules are very clear. Wonders cost 2 bg points for each dot in the highest sphere of its effects. They also have 1 Arete for each dot (you can buy more Arete with 1 bg point), 5 quintessence and one effect for each dot.<br /> So, a wonder with a Life 4+Forces 2 effect, a Correspondence 3 effect, a Forces 1 effect and a Prime 3 effect would cost 8 background points because of the Life 4 effect, would have Arete 4 and 20 quintessence.<br /> <br /> About the points system described in the background section, there is absolutely no sense in that and I advise you to just ignore it and go by the rules on the wonder section.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for 6 freebies you get an Arete 3 Prime 2 Forces 3 &quot;wand of fireblast&quot; that shoots an Aggravated fire attack. Add another 7 freebies and it has Arete 10. Now no ST would allow an Arete 10 Wonder (the implication is that it was created by a Mage with Arete 10, meaning it will be one of a kind and impossibly powerful, so a PC would only have it if it were a mcguffin for the plot), but it's technically legal so eh.<br /> <br /> Now what difficulty are these 10 dice rolled against? I'm imagining difficulty 7 since it's level 3 + 4 for Vulgar No Witnesses. Difficulty 6 if the reality zone is accepting. And Difficulty 6 almost everywhere if our Wand is instead a Flamethrower or low-tech-seeming electricity/energy-based weapon. That is going to average out to about 5 successes, which is 10+ health levels of damage.<br /> <br /> RAW this system seems completely broken. Improving the Arete (even if it is an optional system) makes the item absurdly powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T20:25:41-08:00","id":1294302,"title":"","content":"Yes, but that is not so far from a mage with Arete 3 spending a WP and Quintessence to use Forces to blast 10 aggravated damage. Magick is that powerful, the example I gave cab be done with an initial mage and only spending Wp and quint, no need for 13 freebies points.<br /> <br /> Actually, if the player wants to spend almosball of his freebies in a deadly flamethrower I think the ST should let him. There are ways to avoid that, i don't think it's so overpowered. Magick is overpowered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:12:41-08:00","id":1294448,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I greatly preferred the requisitions system in guide to the technocracy, where it was more of a 'Roll and spend successes to get extra gear for a mission.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:51:43-08:00","id":1294599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1285676-dots-points-and-the-wonder-background?p=1294448#post1294448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I greatly preferred the requisitions system in guide to the technocracy, where it was more of a 'Roll and spend successes to get extra gear for a mission.'</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 still has that with the Requisitions Background. And yeah, it technically makes sense for a Technocrat - after all, the Wonders were already built *for* you. You just, ahem, lend them. Including weird experimental gadgets if you are not in good favors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}